-- Regression test for lexical section scoping — FIX D must not lose a
-- differently-typed overload defined BELOW the reference (spec §12).
--
-- `big` over NUMBER is an ancestor of the reference in §§ users; `big` over
-- STRING is defined in a LATER sibling section with no signature at all, so
-- at the reference it is not yet inferred. The reference `big "hello"` cannot
-- use the ancestor, and the per-type rule (spec §3.3.4 step 4) keeps the
-- sibling overload visible to type-directed resolution. Deferral preserves
-- that: the ancestor fails, the deferred candidate is consulted, and the
-- reference resolves to strings.big.

§ ops
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
big n MEANS n GREATER THAN 10

§§ users
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
test MEANS big "hello"

§§ strings
big s MEANS s EQUALS "hello"

#EVAL ops.users.test   -- TRUE
